# Shared Hugging Face model table: seven TAB-separated columns.
# value name pipeline_tag domain free_tag version path
#
# FoldMason selects free_tag=foldmason-prostt5 and version=gguf-f16-2025-02-26.
# The version identifies the compatible model artifact, not the tool release.
# The original model is https://huggingface.co/Rostlab/ProstT5 (MIT).
# This release needs the converted GGUF weights, not Hugging Face Transformers files.
#
# Download and extract once on the Galaxy reference-data filesystem:
#   foldseek databases ProstT5 /data/models/prostt5-gguf /data/tmp/prostt5
# The archive URL used by that command is:
#   https://foldseek.steineggerlab.workers.dev/prostt5-f16-gguf.tar.gz
# Download size: 2,224,976,412 bytes. Ensure sufficient space for extraction.
# The path column may point to prostt5-f16.gguf or to its containing directory.
# Workers and containers must be able to read this path.
# Merge the example row into the shared huggingface.loc file; retain other tools' rows.
# Schema: https://galaxyproject.org/news/2026-04-13-huggingface-data-table/
#
# foldmason-prostt5-gguf-f16-2025-02-26	ProstT5 GGUF f16 (2025-02-26)	translation	biology	foldmason-prostt5	gguf-f16-2025-02-26	/data/models/prostt5-gguf
